From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: SHRestricted reads machine policy from HKLM first

"Apply policies" (Group Policy). Windows evaluates a shell restriction from the
machine's policy in HKLM as well as the user's in HKCU, and the machine value
wins -- that is what makes a policy an administrator sets binding on every user.
Upstream Wine's SHRestricted read only
HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Policies, so a machine-wide
policy could not be expressed and any user could set their own.

SHRestricted now reads HKLM first; if the machine sets the restriction, that
value is returned (and cached) and HKCU is not consulted. Otherwise HKCU is
read as before. On Stained Glass the HKLM policy branch is administrator-owned
(wine-sg 0024), so an ordinary user cannot plant a machine policy; the
combination gives Windows' precedence with Windows' protection. The cache and
the HKCU path are otherwise unchanged, so ordinary Wine with no HKLM policy set
behaves exactly as before.
--- a/dlls/shell32/shpolicy.c
+++ b/dlls/shell32/shpolicy.c
@@ -849,6 +849,26 @@
 
 	/* return 0 and don't set the cache if any registry errors occur */
 	retval = 0;
+	/* Stained Glass OS: machine policy first. Windows reads this restriction
+	 * from HKLM (the machine's Group Policy) as well as HKCU, and the machine
+	 * value takes precedence over the user's -- that is what makes a policy an
+	 * administrator sets binding on everyone. Upstream Wine read HKCU only, so
+	 * a machine-wide policy could not be expressed. HKLM\Software\Policies is
+	 * administrator-owned here (wine-sg 0024), so an ordinary user cannot
+	 * plant one. */
+	{
+	  DWORD mval = 0, msize = 4;
+	  if (RegOpenKeyA(HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE, regstr, &xhkey) == ERROR_SUCCESS)
+	  {
+	    if (RegQueryValueExA(xhkey, p->keystr, NULL, NULL, (LPBYTE)&mval, &msize) == ERROR_SUCCESS)
+	    {
+	      p->cache = mval;
+	      RegCloseKey(xhkey);
+	      return mval;
+	    }
+	    RegCloseKey(xhkey);
+	  }
+	}
 	if (RegOpenKeyA(HKEY_CURRENT_USER, regstr, &xhkey) == ERROR_SUCCESS)
 	{
 	  if (RegQueryValueExA(xhkey, p->keystr, NULL, NULL, (LPBYTE)&retval, &datsize) == ERROR_SUCCESS)
